nd runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VuePacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Readonly"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ShallowRef"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueRateLimiter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRateLimitedState } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst [count, setCount, utility] = useRateLimitedState(0, { limit: 3, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nsetCount((previous) => previous + 1)\n// Bind count and utility.state in the component. Read count.value for the committed value.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useRateLimiter"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"initialvalue","text":"initialValue","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedState<TValue, TSelected>(\n   initialValue,\n   options,\n   selector?): [Readonly<ShallowRef<TValue>>, SetValue<TValue>, VueRateLimiter<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedState.ts:38](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/vue-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedState.ts#L38)\n\nCreates rate-limited state with a scheduled setter.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, setValue, utility]. The value is a readonly shallow ref; read value.value in JavaScript or bind the ref in a template. Setters accept a value or a functional updater. Updaters run when the utility executes, using the last committed value. Pending updates may be replaced or rejected according to the utility's scheduling rules. To store a function itself, pass an updater that returns that function.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component setup or in an active effect scope. Scope disposal removes watchers and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### initialValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### options\n\n[`VuePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md)\\<[`VueRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Readonly`\\<`ShallowRef`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`VueRateLimiter`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useRateLimitedState } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst [count, setCount, utility] = useRateLimitedState(0, { limit: 3, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nsetCount((previous) => previous + 1)\n// Bind count and utility.state in the component. Read count.value for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseRateLimiter\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useRateLimitedState\ntitle: useRateLimitedState\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedState<TValue, TSelected>(\n   initialValue,\n   options,\n   selector?): [Readonly<ShallowRef<TValue>>, SetValue<TValue>, VueRateLimiter<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedState.ts:38](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/vue-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedState.ts#L38)\n\nCreates rate-limited state with a scheduled setter.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, setValue, utility]. The value is a readonly shallow ref; read value.value in JavaScript or bind the ref in a template. Setters accept a value or a functional updater. Updaters run when the utility executes, using the last committed value. Pending updates may be replaced or rejected according to the utility's scheduling rules. To store a function itself, pass an updater that returns that function.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component setup or in an active effect scope. Scope disposal removes watchers and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### initialValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### options\n\n[`VuePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md)\\<[`VueRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Readonly`\\<`ShallowRef`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`VueRateLimiter`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { useRateLimitedState } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst [count, setCount, utility] = useRateLimitedState(0, { limit: 3, window: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount }),\n)\nsetCount((previous) => previous + 1)\n// Bind count and utility.state in the component. Read count.value for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseRateLimiter\n"}
